IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-payment`

-- Tests of oa2-part2-payment: sections 16 to 18.2. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the words of the
-- section, with the reasoning in the comment.

§ `Section 16 -- consideration and notice`

-- (1): an application under 11(2) or a waiver under 11(3.1) or (4) starts the duty; neither does not.
#ASSERT `s 16(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid a supplement` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid a supplement` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 16(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid a supplement` FALSE FALSE
-- (2): the two duties to notify.
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the basis on which the amount was fixed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 16(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the basis on which the amount was fixed` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the decision that no supplement may be paid and the Minister's reasons` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 16(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the decision that no supplement may be paid and the Minister's reasons` FALSE

§ `Section 17 -- payment in arrears`

-- Ordinary: March 2024 is paid at the end of March; the first month payable is January 2024, approved on January 20.
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 1 20))'s `the earliest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 1 20))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- Approved on January 31, the last day of the first month: not "after the end of" it, so still ordinary.
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 1 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 1 31))'s `the earliest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 1 31)
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 1 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 1 31))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 1 31)
-- Approved on February 1: after the end of January. January's payment may be made at the end of February (leap year:
-- February 29) or at the end of March (March 31).
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 1 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 2 1))'s `the earliest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 1 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 2 1))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
-- Late approval on March 15: the months up to and including March are paid at the end of March or of April; April is
-- ordinary again.
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 2 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 3 15))'s `the earliest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 3 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 3 15))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 4 30)
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 4 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 3 15))'s `the earliest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 4 30)
#ASSERT (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` (YMD 2024 4 10) (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2024 3 15))'s `the latest day` EQUALS (YMD 2024 4 30)

§ `Section 18 -- adjustment`

-- (a): actual income 20000 exceeds shown income 10000; 3000 was paid; at the actual income it would have been 2400:
-- 3000 - 2400 = 600 is deducted and retained.
#ASSERT `s 18(a): the amount to be deducted and retained out of subsequent payments of supplement or pension` 20000 10000 3000 2400 EQUALS 600
-- Not exceeding: nothing. Equal: nothing. A shortfall (the supplement at the actual income would be MORE): nothing is
-- deducted, never a negative.
#ASSERT `s 18(a): the amount to be deducted and retained out of subsequent payments of supplement or pension` 10000 20000 3000 2400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 18(a): the amount to be deducted and retained out of subsequent payments of supplement or pension` 10000 10000 3000 3000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 18(a): the amount to be deducted and retained out of subsequent payments of supplement or pension` 20000 10000 2400 3000 EQUALS 0
-- (b) as written: the shown income 20000 exceeds the actual income 10000; 2400 was paid on the shown income; the
-- supplement "if the actual income had been equal to the shown income" is the same 2400, so the difference is nothing.
#ASSERT `s 18(b): the amount to be paid to the applicant, read as it is written` 10000 20000 2400 2400 EQUALS 0
-- (b) read as the mirror of (a): at the actual income the supplement would have been 3000; 3000 - 2400 = 600 is paid.
#ASSERT `s 18(b): the amount to be paid to the applicant, read as the mirror of paragraph (a)` 10000 20000 2400 3000 EQUALS 600
-- Shown income not exceeding the actual income: nothing under (b). A supplement already above what it would be: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 18(b): the amount to be paid to the applicant, read as the mirror of paragraph (a)` 20000 10000 2400 3000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 18(b): the amount to be paid to the applicant, read as the mirror of paragraph (a)` 10000 20000 3000 2400 EQUALS 0

§ `Section 18.1 -- request that the supplement cease`

-- The Minister approves in March 2024: ceases on the last day of March, March 31.
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the last day of the month on which the supplement ceases to be payable` (YMD 2024 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2024 3 31)
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the last day of the month on which the supplement ceases to be payable` (YMD 2024 2 15) EQUALS (YMD 2024 2 29)
-- Resumes at the later of the month after the month of the new application and the month chosen. New application in May
-- 2024: June 1. Chosen September 2024: September 1 is later. Chosen April 2024: June 1 is later.
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the first month in which the supplement may resume` (YMD 2024 5 20) (YMD 2024 9 3) EQUALS (YMD 2024 9 1)
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the first month in which the supplement may resume` (YMD 2024 5 20) (YMD 2024 4 3) EQUALS (YMD 2024 6 1)
-- Chosen the month after the application's month exactly: the same month.
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the first month in which the supplement may resume` (YMD 2024 5 20) (YMD 2024 6 1) EQUALS (YMD 2024 6 1)
-- Payable for a month: request made, approved in March 2024, may resume in September 2024.
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` (YMD 2024 2 10) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 1))
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` (YMD 2024 3 31) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` (YMD 2024 4 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` (YMD 2024 8 31) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 1))
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` (YMD 2024 9 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 1))
-- No new application yet: never resumes. No request: payable.
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2024 3 10) NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` (YMD 2024 4 1) FALSE (YMD 2024 3 10) NOTHING

§ `Section 18.2 -- cancellation`

-- Payment commenced January 15, 2024; the prescribed time is taken to be six months (Regulations s 26.1 is oa3's):
-- the last day is July 15, 2024.
#ASSERT `s 18.2(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the supplement` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 15) (`a limit in months` 6) (YMD 2024 7 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.2(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the supplement` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 15) (`a limit in months` 6) (YMD 2024 7 16)
#ASSERT `s 18.2(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the supplement` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 15) (`a limit in months` 6) (YMD 2024 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.2(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the supplement` TRUE (YMD 2024 1 15) (`a limit in months` 6) (YMD 2024 1 14)
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.2(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the supplement` FALSE (YMD 2024 1 15) (`a limit in months` 6) (YMD 2024 2 1)
-- (2): both the grant and the repayment in time are needed for either deemed effect.
#ASSERT `s 18.2(2)(a): the application for the supplement is deemed never to have been made` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.2(2)(a): the application for the supplement is deemed never to have been made` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.2(2)(a): the application for the supplement is deemed never to have been made` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18.2(2)(b): the supplement is deemed not to have been payable during the period in question` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.2(2)(b): the supplement is deemed not to have been payable during the period in question` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 18.2(2)(b): the supplement is deemed not to have been payable during the period in question` FALSE FALSE
